---
config:
  flowchart:
    wrappingWidth: 400
---
flowchart TB
    accTitle: How the dashboard reaches its readers
    accDescr: Every two hours, after a change of the changelog and on demand, the Dashboard workflow runs dashboard.py, which reads what GitHub shows of every public repository of the owner: its releases, pull requests, runs and reports, and its Scorecard. It writes the page and beside it the same data as repos.json, the health of each day as history.json and the 30 newest releases as the Atom feed releases.atom. GitHub Pages publishes them at addresses that stay, and the job that publishes asks for each file. People read the page, the owner's website reads repos.json, and feed readers follow releases.atom.

    start["Every two hours · a change of the changelog<br>on demand"]
    collect["dashboard.py<br>what GitHub shows of every repository<br>releases · pull requests · runs · Scorecard"]
    page["index.html<br>the page"]
    data["repos.json<br>the same data"]
    history["history.json<br>the health of each day"]
    feed["releases.atom<br>the 30 newest releases"]
    pages["GitHub Pages<br>/repo-blueprint/dashboard/<br>asked for each file"]
    people["People"]
    hub["The owner's website"]
    readers["Feed readers"]

    start --> collect
    collect --> page
    collect --> data
    collect --> history
    collect --> feed
    page --> pages
    data --> pages
    history --> pages
    feed --> pages
    pages --> people
    pages --> hub
    pages --> readers

    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    classDef person fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    class collect bot
    class page,data,history,feed,pages done
    class people,hub,readers person
